ishikawa-beta
    The Evolution of Artificial Intelligence (1936-2025)
    Transformer Era (2017-2025)
        2017: Transformer — Attention Is All You Need
        2022: ChatGPT — 100M users in 2 months
        2024: OpenAI o1 — chain-of-thought reasoning
    Modern Deep Learning (2012-2016)
        2012: AlexNet — deep learning revolution
        2014: GANs — Goodfellow, generative AI born
        2016: AlphaGo — defeats Lee Sedol 4-1
    Deep Learning Renaissance (2006-2011)
        2006: Deep Belief Networks — Hinton
        2007: NVIDIA CUDA — GPU for AI
        2011: IBM Watson wins Jeopardy!
    Statistical AI Rise (1994-2005)
        1997: Deep Blue — defeats Kasparov
        1997: LSTM — Hochreiter & Schmidhuber
        2005: DARPA Challenge — Stanley wins
    Second AI Winter (1987-1993)
        1988: Bayesian Networks — Judea Pearl
        1989: LeNet CNN — Yann LeCun
    Expert Systems Era (1980-1987)
        1980: XCON/R1 — first expert system at DEC
        1982: Hopfield Networks — NN revived
        1986: Back-prop — Rumelhart, Hinton, Williams
    First AI Winter (1970-1979)
        1973: Lighthill Report — UK funding cut
        1974: Back-propagation — Werbos PhD
    Birth of AI (1956-1969)
        1956: Dartmouth Conference — AI born
        1957: Perceptron — Frank Rosenblatt
        1966: ELIZA — first chatbot
    Foundations of Computing (1936-1955)
        1936: Universal Turing Machine
        1950: The Turing Test
        1955: AI term coined — McCarthy
